---
component: reading
params:
  sky: { type: { enum: [clear, fog, storm] }, default: "@sky" }
  hour: string
---

## Readings

@narrator: {{@hour}}. You unlatch the white louvred box and read down the column, the way Ines taught you.

<match on="@sky">
  <when is="clear">
    @narrator: Dry bulb seventeen point two. Wet bulb thirteen. Pressure steady, a hair above yesterday.
    @narrator: The sky is the hard blue it only is at altitude.
  </when>
  <when is="fog">
    @narrator: The louvres drip. Visibility, you guess, forty metres; you cannot see the funicular mast.
    @narrator: Humidity pinned at the top of the dial. The fog tastes of iron.
  </when>
  <when is="storm">
    @narrator: The barograph pen has dropped off the bottom of the drum.
    @narrator: Rain drives sideways under the eaves and into the box before you can shut it.
  </when>
</match>
